 "trace": {
  "face.shapes.dots": "Each dot a circle of r 0.045 (rect with full corner radius) instead of a 12-point polygon, which the smooth-edge check reads as a 2 mm wobble.",
  "cab.doors[0]": "Cab door 1.56..2.19 m (x 1.875, w 0.63): its recessed seam on p258 (u 1801-1897 at v 1250-1550), read through a bodyside homography fitted on the 12 window-frame corners of p258.json (rms 3 px). The 317 template drew it 1.30..2.18 m, its front edge over the cab side window.",
  "nose.glazing": "Tall fixed cab side window ahead of the cab door: frame 0.84..1.34 m by 1.72..3.08 m on p258 (corners u 1668/1758 v 1112, u 1680/1767 v 1510, same homography); glass drawn 3 cm inside the frame. Not on the 317 diagram. Needs fromSpec (classes/bremu.ts) to pass nose.glazing through.",
  "cab.doors[1..2]": "Passenger doors: the opening in the bodyside, front jamb to the rear jamb's outer edge, 5.81..7.11 m (door 1) and 12.90..14.09 m (door 2) on p258 through the homography: w 1.30 (published clear opening 1.010 m; the 317 template drew 1.768) and both 0.12 m ahead of the template (6.45, 13.51). Leaf windows 0.20..0.56 m from the centre line (rear leaf, 6.49..6.89 against the seam 6.27 and leaf edge 6.99, scaled to a 0.65 leaf), 2.09..3.02 m high.",
  "next.doors": "Width, panes and window as the cab car's doors; positions kept from the template (car 2 not measured).",
  "face.heights": "Every face height scaled by 0.92 about 3.40 m (the orange arc's ends at the corners): the face was drawn from p254 at the horizontal px/m, but p254 is taken from well left of the axis (the headlamp lens reads 75 px across, 80 px up), so its vertical scale is ~8% larger. Both camera matches want it (a screen-height scale fitted with the cameras: 0.913 on p258 and p265), and the side/face cameras put the lamp centres at 1.43-1.52 m (facesolve p258, p265; the p258 bodyside homography at the corner puts the housing at 1.43-1.59).",
  "face.panel": "Yellow 1.11..2.24 m: its top 19 px (5 cm at p254's ~409 px/m vertical) below the windscreen glass, its depth 461 px (1.13 m) on p254; the p258 bodyside homography at the corner reads 1.03-1.09..2.31-2.33.",
  "face.screens[1]": "Gangway door glass 0.87 m wide (330 px at p254's 378.6 px/m across) and its top 13 px (3 cm) below the windscreens' tops on p254: 2.284..3.32 m; p265's camera also put the old 3.21 m top 7 cm low.",
  "face.gangway": "No `gangway`: on this pipeline a face gangway door gets a 0.2 m studded rubber surround (pipeline/blender/body.py), which the 318's flush gangway door has none of (p254, p258, p265). The door is the yellow of the panel, its edges the seam in `lines` (bottom 1.13, 2 cm above the yellow's lower edge).",
  "face.number": "On the near side (image right on p254, p258, p265, where the close view puts m < 0): centre 352 px right of the face centre on p254 (0.93 m at 378.6 px/m), 0.44 m under the yellow's top, letters 45 px (0.11 m) high.",
  "liveries.SR.branding": "The ScotRail logo (logos/SR.svg: saltire of dots, 'ScotRail', 'Scotland's Railway'; the bodyside vinyl is the same layout in one colour, a trace off p258 squared up gives an ink box of aspect 2.96 against the artwork's 2.89), between doors 1 and 2 below the windows, saltire towards the cab on the near side (p258) and turned round on the far side (p304, on the 320). Cab car: its extremes on p258 through the bodyside homography (window-frame corners, rms 3 px) run 8.96..11.25 m, so 2.29 m wide, centre x 10.10; 'ScotRail' 1.33..1.74 m, centre y 1.53. The lettering reads 0.41 m tall, and the saltire 0.86-0.95 m tall (p258 trace squared up; its faint end dots read short): 0.90 m high, with `width` 2.29 because the vinyl is squatter than the artwork (aspect 2.54 against 2.89; the lettering 0.34 m at that height against 0.41 read). A trace from a side-on photo would settle it (none on Commons; p258's is too foreshortened to trace cleanly). Second car: carried mid-car too (p304, on the 320's MSO and TSO), placed in the middle of the gap between its doors at the same height; not measured. Colour: the white of the saltire dots (p258: lettering 198,201,204 beside the cab dots 214,219,223)."
 },
